Help the user get toolbox-db working. Work through this in order, checking state before
suggesting anything — do not dump the whole guide at them.

## 1. Is a Toolbox server running?

```bash
curl -sS -m 5 "${TOOLBOX_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:5000}/api/toolset" >/dev/null && echo reachable || echo "not reachable"
```

If not reachable, the user needs the MCP Toolbox server (a Go binary, separate from this plugin):
- install: <https://mcp-toolbox.dev/getting-started/introduction/>
- run: `./toolbox --tools-file tools.yaml` (defaults to port 5000)

A minimal `tools.yaml` for Postgres — offer to write one if they don't have it:

```yaml
sources:
  my-pg:
    kind: postgres
    host: 127.0.0.1
    port: 5432
    database: mydb
    user: ${DB_USER}
    password: ${DB_PASSWORD}

tools:
  search-users:
    kind: postgres-sql
    source: my-pg
    description: Find users whose email matches a pattern.
    parameters:
      - name: email_pattern
        type: string
        description: SQL LIKE pattern, e.g. '%@example.com'
    statement: SELECT id, email, created_at FROM users WHERE email LIKE $1 LIMIT 100;

toolsets:
  default:
    - search-users
```

Database credentials belong in `tools.yaml` (or the Toolbox server's own environment), not in
this plugin — the plugin only talks to the Toolbox server.

## 2. Session environment variables

These are read by the plugin's MCP server at launch. Tell the user to export them in the shell
*before* starting Claude Code (fish syntax, since that's their shell):

```fish
set -gx TOOLBOX_URL http://127.0.0.1:5000
set -gx TOOLBOX_TOOLSET default        # optional; omit for the default toolset
```

Auth, only if their Toolbox server requires it:

```fish
set -gx TOOLBOX_API_KEY "…"                       # sent as Authorization: Bearer …
set -gx TOOLBOX_GOOGLE_ID_TOKEN 1                 # Cloud Run: mint a Google ID token instead
set -gx TOOLBOX_AUTH_TOKENS '{"my_auth":"eyJ…"}'  # per-tool auth services
set -gx TOOLBOX_BOUND_PARAMS '{"tenant_id":"42"}' # values pinned on every call
```

The full list is in `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/README.md`.

## 3. Verify

```bash
node "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/doctor.mjs"
```

Environment variables are captured when Claude Code starts, so newly exported ones only take
effect after restarting Claude Code from the shell that has them. Once it restarts, confirm the
database tools appear (`toolbox_status`). Changes made to `tools.yaml` on the Toolbox server side
need only the `toolbox_reload` tool.

